	(text "GND"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 26.67 128.27 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "d9c952df-7a68-4f21-b5e4-83abb05eb3b1")
	)
	(text "PH = DIR, EN = PWM. EN low = brake (both low sides on).\nnSLEEP low = FETs held off; its internal 115k pull-down\nkeeps the bridge off during a reset or the bootloader.\nFirmware: nSLEEP high once MOTOR_SW is up, PWM 1 ms\nlater; nFAULT: MCU pull-up on.\n\nCurrent limit, cycle by cycle: R27 + R28 = 4 mOhm in\nthe low-side return (LS_SRC), Kelvin taps to SP / SN.\nVREF = 5 V x 3.3k / 13.3k = 1.22 V (+5V: tighter than\nAVDD, 4.4-5.2 V). ICHOP = (VREF - VOFF) / (20 x 4 mOhm)\n= 14.6 A typ. with VOFF = 50 mV; 9.5 to 18 A worst case\n(VOFF up to 250 mV, gain 18-24). Above ICHOP the bridge\nbrakes for 25 us, then drives again. R30 = 4.7k: 19 A.\nTP14 = SO = VOFF + 80 mV/A while driving; SO = VOFF\nwhen the bridge is awake and stopped.\nThe INA226 still measures the supply current and cuts\nthe PWM and Q5. The DRV8701 also trips at 1 V VDS.\n\nJ7: 7.62 mm pluggable header, so the 5.08 mm 24 V plug\nof J1 / J5 cannot go into the motor output.\nIDRIVE open: 100 mA source / 200 mA sink.\nBypass with an external driver on J5 / J6: cut JP2-JP5\nand the JP6 wire link (1.5 mm2, hand-soldered)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 180.34 211.455 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "dc4f551e-2010-4ef0-a076-36d4476414ac")
	)
